A||||27||ChadMan||I hate people -- resolution (in which ChadMan learns to calm down)||||9||
Z||000000||ChadMan||07-18-2001||04:16 PM||||My wife calls me at work today and asks me to come home for lunch.  I do, and when I get there, my neighbor (an elderly Indian man) is unloading his car - he's been gone since Sunday morning.  I ask him if he saw anybody hit my car, and he says no and comes over to look at the damage.  (see <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008828.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008828.html</A>  for the whole story)<P>He gets down and looks at it closely and this shocked look comes over his face.  "Oh no," he says, "maybe it WAS me..."  He goes over and looks at his own car, and sure enough, his right-front bumper is scuffed.  "Oh no...it WAS me.  I own it...I own it..."  (His English isn't the best.)<P>Well, I'm standing there looking at this frail, friendly old Indian guy with bad vision and his hands up saying "I own it," and all of a sudden I'm not angry anymore.  I hear myself telling him it's an old car and not to worry about it.  (Three trophies at FOCOA national meets, and I'm telling him not to worry about crashing into my Fiero.)<P>He is visibly relieved and insists that I come over for a beer after work.  So tonight I will go drink my neighbor's beer, and Saturday I will do my best to buff this big uglyassed scuff off of my car.  And for some reason, I feel ashamed for being so mad about it.  Am I right just to let this go, or am I a big fat pushover?<P>All I know is -- no nice Fiero for me until I have a garage to put it in.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Jay||07-18-2001||04:24 PM||||Chadman I think you were right in what you did.  Sometimes to have a good relationship is worth more than a paint chip or scratch.  I've felt that way myself.  I mean what are you gonna do...crack the old guy over the head?  I for one applaude what you did, and you know what?  you are a better person for it!  Yeah I know I sound like I'm a gearbox but it's okay.  I'm all man, fighting doesn't accomplish anything except make enemies.  For over six months I had a beef with my neighbours, I was relieved when they finally moved, the new ones are okay but it was hell trying to avoid my neighbours all the time (our drive ways are attatched).  Good for you!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||07-18-2001||04:32 PM||||Everybody give ChadMan a big pat on the back.<BR>:: patta-patta-pat ::<P>There you go.  <BR>Simma-down.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 07-18-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||DRH||07-18-2001||04:38 PM||||Just shows you're a good person. Nothing wrong with that. I would do exactly the same thing under the circumstances.<P>Now if he were some a$$hole that said 'so what?' it would be a whole different story.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||07-18-2001||04:40 PM||||When I lived in Iowa I had a beat up old VW bug I drove to work. <P> in the winter the parking lots were frozen about 6" deep with ice - and the sun came out one day, and about half the cars in the parking lot slid across the lot during day all by themselves - about 50 cars were all bunched up one side of the lot. It was the weirdist thing.<P>  someones car had slid into the rear fender of my bug and dented it a little. The owner was there when I came out, backed his car away, and was apologizing, insisting he would pay for the dent (I dont know why - it wasnt his fault).<P>  I looked at the dent for a second, said, "wait a minute" and i walked around to the other side of the car and kick the other rear fender.<P>  then I walked back and told the guy "there - all fixed - now its symectrical again" and I smiled and drove off.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Butter||07-18-2001||04:48 PM||||Human compassion is in short supply.  You have improved the supply.  Good for You!<P>It's just stuff. People are what really matters.||||reg||7
Z||000006||fierojunky||07-18-2001||04:56 PM||||Your a better man then me.  I would have been all over him like 84Bill on the Fierolisa thread.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000007||Fierochic88||07-18-2001||06:05 PM||||Good job Chad!  I doubt I would have remained composed, but then again I have a soft spot for little old men.<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||07-18-2001||06:37 PM||||Bravo!<BR>I *do* believe that what goes around comes around. <BR>In the grand scheme of things, your act of kindness will not go unnoticed. <BR>Karma. Or whatever.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000009||hugh||07-18-2001||07:41 PM||||Over the years I have been unfortunate enough to have been in the same situation a few times.I can only describe the feeling I got as relief from being mad about something I couldn't control.I wasn't happy but even though my car(s)were not going to be the same I could accept it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||maryjane||07-18-2001||08:01 PM||||My hats off to you Chadman, ya did the right thing. Acts such as your's usually have a way of being returned when least expected||||reg||1
Z||000011||AusFiero||07-18-2001||08:04 PM||||Yes you did well Chadman. One of the many parking lot scuffs I have had the old guy waited for me to try pay for it. He was in a beat up Beetle, I was in a brand new car. I figured he couldn't afford to pay for it so I just said hey, sheet happens mate, at least you was honest enough to wait. <P>Weeks later I seen him in my local RSL (Retired Servicemans League) club and I actually had a great time sitting down with all the old WWII vets while he bought me a beer and I heard stories I would have never heard otherwise.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
